  "description": "Binary-to-text encodings for .NET 8 and .NET 10 - Base16, Base32, Base45, Base58, Base62, Base64, Base85, and Bech32, plus percent-encoding and quoted-printable - with a uniform static API, variant selection, encode-time formatting options, and decode-time leniency styles. The five core encodings (Base16, Base32, Base58, Base64, Base85) expose span, string, UTF-8, and IBufferWriter surfaces with Try* and length-calculation overloads for allocation-free use.",
